<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13610" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπορρήγνῡμι</span></b>  or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ύω,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>break off,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεσμὸν ἀπορρήξας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.507
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.32
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἧκε δ᾽ ἀπορρήξας κορυφὴν ὄρεος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					9.481
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πνεῦμ᾽ ἀπέρρηξεν βίου</span>
			<i>snap the thread</i> of life, <i>die,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				507
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πνεῦμα, βίον,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				864
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IT</u>
				974
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tr.</u>
				756
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ψυχήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.313
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ μακρὰ τείχη ἀ. ἀπὸ τῆς τῶν
					Μεγαρέων πόλεως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					4.69
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τῆς εἰρήνης τὴν
			ξυμμαχίαν,</span> a phrase of <i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i> censured by <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				3.72
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πάνυ τείνουσαι τὸ καλῴδιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>DMeretr.</u>
					3.3
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> causal,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τὸν θυμόν</span>
			<i>let</i> one's rage <i>burst forth,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				9.5
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Am.</u>
				43
			</span></i>; <i>burst out with</i> a remark, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>BC</u>
				2.81
			</span></i>: —
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλεμος . . ἀπερρήγνυτο ἐς ἔργον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Syr.</u>
					15
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἑαυτόν τινος</span>
			<i>tear</i> oneself <i>away, break away</i> from, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Marc.</u>
				27
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν τοῦ πατρὸς ἐπιτηδευμάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					10.3.1
				</span></i>
			; <i>deprive,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς ἀδελφοὺς τῆς βασιλικῆς ἐλπίδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>BJ</u>
					1.23.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, freq. in aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπερράγην [ᾰ</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.19
			</span></i>,etc.:pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπέρρηγμαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.510
				</span></i>
			; but 3sg.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπορέρηκται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				46.21.22
			</span></i>:—<i>to be broken off or severed from,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπό τιϝος</span> Hdt.l.c., ib.<i><span class="en">
				37
			</span></i>: abs., <i>to be broken off, severed,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.29
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				5.10
			</span></i>, etc.; <i>break away from</i> one's allegiance, <i>rebel,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>BJ</u>
				2.14.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				Act.
			, pf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπέρρωγα</span> in 
				Pass.
			 sense, <i><span class="en">
				Archil.
				47
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φωνὴ ἀπερρωγυῖα</span> a
				<i>broken</i> voice, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i>
			<i>Acut.(Sp.)</i><i><span class="en">
				10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Aud.</u>
				804b20
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπερρωγώς</span>”
				<i>broken in character, dissolute,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Pseudol.</u>
					17
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἵ γε μὴ τελέως -ότες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Muson.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					12p.64H.
				</span></i>
			; <i>absurd,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				8.165
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> intr. in
				aor. 1
			
				Act.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπορρήξας ἀπὸ δεσμῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.240
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Phil.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακὸν ἀπέρρηξε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Abd.</u>
					6
				</span></i>
			.</div>
